<!-- Header -->
<%- include("partials/header.ejs") %>

  <main>
    <h2>Where AI is used today</h2>
    <p>AI is rarely a product on its own. It gets built into something that already exists, so the useful question
      is which part of the work it takes over.</p>

    <table>
      <caption>A few common examples of AI in everyday work</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr id="table-header">
          <th scope="col">Field</th>
          <th scope="col">What the AI does</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="table-row">
          <td>Health care</td>
          <td>Marks suspicious areas on a scan for a doctor to check</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="table-row">
          <td>Transport</td>
          <td>Spots lanes, signs and obstacles in real time</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="table-row">
          <td>Factories</td>
          <td>Finds broken parts on a line faster than a person can look</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="table-row">
          <td>Language</td>
          <td>Drafts, summarises and translates text</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- Faker data -->
    <h2>AI Team</h2>
    <p>Here are some of our experts. The data is generated with the Faker.js package and changes on every refresh.</p>

    <table>
      <caption>All these companies use AI to better support their work</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr class="table-head">
          <th scope="col">Name</th>
          <th scope="col">Job title</th>
          <th scope="col">Company</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% team.forEach(member => { %>
        <tr class="table-row">
          <td><%= member.name %></td>
          <td><%= member.role %></td>
          <td><%= member.company %></td>
        </tr>
        <% }); %>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <figure>
      <img src="/img/robot-arm.jpg" alt="A robot arm in a factory picking up metal cylinders">
      <figcaption>A robot arm checking parts in a factory</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Problems to watch for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bias:</strong> a model learns from data, so it also copies the unfairness in that data.</li>
      <li><strong>Made up answers:</strong> language models produce the most likely next words, not checked facts,
        so anything important has to be checked somewhere else.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> text sent to a chat tool may be stored, so passwords and personal details do
        not belong in a prompt.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <ul class="sources">
      <li><a href="https://www.nist.gov/itl/ai-risk-management-framework" target="_blank">NIST: AI Risk Management
          Framework</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.propublica.org/article/machine-bias-risk-assessments-in-criminal-sentencing"
          target="_blank">ProPublica: Machine bias</a></li>
    </ul>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <%- include("partials/footer.ejs") %>